# NHS Jobs Search — Functional Acceptance Test Suite

**Candidate:** [Applicant Name]
**Repository:** `[Applicant Name]-NHSBSA`
**Tech Stack:** Java 21 · Selenium 4 · Cucumber 7 · JUnit 5 · Maven · WebDriverManager

---

## Overview

BDD functional acceptance test suite for the NHS Jobs candidate search page:
`https://www.jobs.nhs.uk/candidate/search`

Tests are written in Gherkin from the user's perspective and cover:
- Happy path searches (keyword, location, combinations)
- Sorting results by "Date posted (newest first)"
- Pagination
- Edge cases (empty search, special characters, no results)
- Result card content validation (title, employer, closing date)
- Cross-browser execution (Chrome & Firefox)

---

## Prerequisites

| Requirement | Version |
|-------------|---------|
| Java JDK    | 21+     |
| Maven       | 3.8+    |
| Chrome      | Latest  |
| Firefox     | Latest  |

> **No manual driver download required.**
> [WebDriverManager](https://github.com/bonigarcia/webdrivermanager) automatically resolves,
> downloads, and caches the correct browser driver at runtime.

---

## Quick Start

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/[ApplicantName]/[ApplicantName]-NHSBSA.git
cd [ApplicantName]-NHSBSA
```

### 2. Run all tests (Chrome, headed)

```bash
mvn test
```

---

## Command Line Execution

### Run all tests

```bash
mvn test
```

### Run on Firefox

```bash
mvn test -Dbrowser=firefox
```

### Run on Chrome (explicit)

```bash
mvn test -Dbrowser=chrome
```

### Run headless (CI/CD environments)

```bash
mvn test -Dheadless=true
```

### Run headless on Firefox

```bash
mvn test -Dbrowser=firefox -Dheadless=true
```

### Run only Smoke tests

```bash
mvn test -Dcucumber.tags="@Smoke"
```

### Run only Happy Path tests

```bash
mvn test -Dcucumber.tags="@HappyPath"
```

### Run sort-related tests only

```bash
mvn test -Dcucumber.tags="@SortOrder"
```

### Run all tests on both browsers (sequentially)

```bash
mvn test -Dbrowser=chrome && mvn test -Dbrowser=firefox
```

### Full CI pipeline command

```bash
mvn clean test -Dbrowser=chrome -Dheadless=true
```

---

## Available System Properties

| Property            | Default | Description                          |
|---------------------|---------|--------------------------------------|
| `browser`           | `chrome`| Browser to use: `chrome` or `firefox`|
| `headless`          | `false` | Run browser in headless mode         |
| `cucumber.tags`     | *(all)* | Cucumber tag filter expression       |
| `baseUrl`           | NHS URL | Override the base URL                |

---

## Tag Reference

| Tag              | Description                                      |
|------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| `@Smoke`         | Critical happy-path tests for quick validation   |
| `@HappyPath`     | All positive/expected outcome scenarios          |
| `@SortOrder`     | Tests validating date-posted sort functionality  |
| `@Filters`       | Tests using search filters and parameters        |
| `@Pagination`    | Tests navigating multiple result pages           |
| `@EdgeCase`      | Boundary and negative test scenarios             |
| `@NoResults`     | Tests expecting no results message               |
| `@ResultDetails` | Tests validating content of job result cards     |
| `@DateValidation`| Tests verifying date ordering accuracy           |
| `@Chrome`        | Chrome-specific scenarios                        |
| `@Firefox`       | Firefox-specific scenarios                       |

